---
layout: base.njk
title: Fees
description: Plain pricing, no packages you don't need. Final figures from Sarah.
---
{#- Screen 2c. As on 2a and 2b, title and description are the design's own h1 and
    lead, used verbatim rather than written fresh.

    No contactFooter and no permalink, for the same two reasons as 2b: the compact
    dark footer comes from leaving contactFooter off, and Eleventy maps this file
    to /fees/, which is what header.njk already links to and what makes
    aria-current="page" fire. -#}

{#- TODO-SARAH: the prices. All three are the design's placeholder — a euro sign
    and an em dash, no figure. They stay that way until Sarah gives us numbers;
    a wrong price on a fees page is worse than an obviously absent one.

    A list plus a loop rather than three copy-pasted cards, the same call
    testimonials.njk and header.njk make: the markup is identical every time and
    only the strings differ.

    featured is the one flag that decides which card gets the purple outline and
    the "Most booked" badge. Note this differs from the design, which draws them
    on the mock interview card — moving them is a matter of shifting that one
    word to another entry, and nothing else changes. -#}
{% set services = [
  { name: "Career coaching session",  price: "€—", detail: "60 minutes, one-to-one. Goal setting and next steps.", featured: true },
  { name: "CV & cover letter review", price: "€—", detail: "Written feedback plus a rewritten draft." },
  { name: "Mock interview",           price: "€—", detail: "Realistic practice with structured feedback." }
] %}

<div class="page-head">
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Fees</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lead">Plain pricing, no packages you don't need. Final figures from Sarah.</p>
</div>

{#- A ul where the design has plain divs: three services are a list, and saying so
    gets "list, 3 items" announced before them. The reset it needs is in pages.css,
    as it already is for the nav in base.css. -#}
<ul class="fees">
  {%- for s in services %}

  {#- The badge is real text and comes first, as the design draws it, so the card
      reads "Most booked, Career coaching session". No aria-hidden — unlike the
      quote glyph on 2b it is information, not ornament.

      The price sits outside the h2 rather than inside it. Within the heading it
      would be announced as part of the name — "Career coaching session, euro
      dash" — so the row is a wrapper and the heading holds the name alone. -#}
  <li class="card{% if s.featured %} card--featured{% endif %}">
    {%- if s.featured %}
    <span class="fee__badge">Most booked</span>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="fee__row">
      <h2 class="card__title">{{ s.name }}</h2>
      <p class="fee__price">{{ s.price }}</p>
    </div>
    <p class="card__note">{{ s.detail }}</p>
  </li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>

{#- The design's button points at screen 2d, so this is the Book page and not the
    homepage's Calendly marker — the same call testimonials.njk made.

    The closing line is a plain paragraph. The design gives it no anchor of any
    kind, so it is not a link. -#}
<div class="fee-cta">
  <a class="button" href="/book/">Book a consultation</a>
  <p class="fee-cta__note">Not sure which fits? Start with the free intro call.</p>
</div>
